position is set to explained, and an independent sourced question is opened on the recovery ballot/authority path that the same code gates on IsLeader.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"s-nack-accept\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"epaxos/epaxos.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1008, \\\"end_line\\\": 1035, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"s-isleader-default\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"epaxos/epaxos.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 149, \\\"end_line\\\": 165, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"s-betheleader\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"epaxos/epaxos.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1121, \\\"end_line\\\": 1125, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"aa497fcd14934325ba2eabe45fefecd1-question-0\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"explained\\\"},\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@rec-recovery-ballot\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\": \\\"Can a recovering replica that is not the master-designated leader recover an instance whose accepted value sits at a ballot above its own recovery ballot, or does the periodic retry repeat the same rejected prepare with no enabled repair?\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s-makeballot\\\", \\\"s-exec-recovery-trigger\\\", \\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\", \\\"s-nack-accept\\\", \\\"s-isleader-default\\\", \\\"s-betheleader\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"makeBallot gives a fixed ballot per replica (r.Id for the instance owner, r.Id+N otherwise) and climbs above maxRecvBallot only while r.IsLeader is true; epaxos.New hardcodes IsLeader false and only the master's BeTheLeader RPC sets it, so for every other replica a prepare at its fixed ballot is rejected by any acceptor whose stored bal is higher, and the three nack repairs (handlePreAcceptReply, handleAcceptReply, handlePrepareReply) are all gated on r.IsLeader. executeCommands re-enqueues the same instance every COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD, so the same rejected prepare is repeated without a ballot advance, and instances that depend on 